Flutter Donations Flow

This plan doubles as a copy-paste-ready Cursor prompt for the Flutter app. The backend (Node.js + MongoDB + Paystack) is already implemented in this repo; this document only describes the client work.

Backend contract (locked, do not change)

Base: ${API_BASE_URL}/api/v1. All endpoints require Authorization: Bearer <Firebase ID token>.





GET /donations — approved + visible donations.



POST /donations/:id/donate — body { amount: number>=10, currency?: "ZAR", note?: string<=280, callbackUrl?: string }. Returns { reference, authorization_url, authorizationUrl, accessCode, publicKey, amount, currency, donation: { _id, title }, contributionId, contributionNumber }.



GET /payments/verify/:reference — idempotent. Returns { status: "success"|"failed"|"abandoned"|"unknown", alreadyPaid, payment, contribution }.



GET /donations/contributions/my?page&limit&paymentStatus — paginated history.

Verify is the only source of truth. The frontend must never trust the Paystack redirect alone.

High-level flow

flowchart LR
  list[DonationsListScreen] --> pick[Donation tap]
  pick --> sheet[DonateAmountSheet]
  sheet --> init["POST /donations/:id/donate"]
  init --> webview[PaystackWebView]
  webview --> verify["GET /payments/verify/:reference"]
  verify -->|success| success[DonationSuccessScreen]
  verify -->|failed/abandoned/unknown| failed[DonationFailedScreen]
  failed --> sheet
  list --> history[MyContributionsScreen]

