Repository API

Future<List<Donation>> listDonations({int page = 1, int limit = 20});
Future<DonationInitData> initiateDonation({
  required String donationId,
  required num amount,
  String currency = 'ZAR',
  String? note,
  String? callbackUrl,
});
Future<VerifyResult> verifyPayment(String reference);
Future<({List<DonationContribution> items, int total, int totalPages})> listMyContributions({
  int page = 1, int limit = 10, String? paymentStatus,
});

Map Dio errors to a typed DonationException exposing status + friendly message from response.data['message'] when present. Accept both authorization_url and authorizationUrl when parsing.

Providers (Riverpod)





donationsRepositoryProvider



donationsListProvider — FutureProvider



myContributionsProvider — FutureProvider.family<…, ContributionsQuery>



donateControllerProvider — AsyncNotifier exposing initiate(...) and verify(reference); holds the current DonationInitData and VerifyResult.

Screens





DonationsListScreen — pulls donationsListProvider. Card per donation with image, title, short description, Donate button. Pull-to-refresh, shimmer loading state, empty state.



DonationDetailsScreen (optional polish) — full image, full description, primary Donate button at the bottom.



DonateAmountSheet (bottom sheet)





Inputs: amount (decimal, min 10), optional 280-char note.



Quick chips: 50, 100, 250, 500, 1000.



Client-side validation mirrors backend (amount >= 10, note <= 280).



On submit → donateController.initiate(...) → push DonationPaystackWebViewScreen with authorizationUrl + reference.



Show inline error from DonationException.message.



Disable submit while in flight; show button-level spinner.



DonationPaystackWebViewScreen





Loads authorization_url in webview_flutter.



Intercept navigation via NavigationDelegate.onNavigationRequest:





Match my callback host (e.g. app.satya.example/donation/return).



Also treat Paystack URLs containing standard/close or standard/success as terminal.



When terminal, prevent navigation and call donateController.verify(reference).



Show full-screen "Confirming your donation…" overlay while verifying.



On isPaid === true → pushReplacement to DonationSuccessScreen.



Otherwise → pushReplacement to DonationFailedScreen.



Android back button: if not yet completed, kick off verify (the user may have paid before closing) before popping.



Retry verify with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s — max 3 attempts) on transient network errors. Backend is idempotent.



DonationSuccessScreen — big green check, donation title, currency amount, contributionNumber, Done → pop to donations list, optional View receipt → My Contributions.



DonationFailedScreen — red icon, status text, reference, Try again → reopens amount sheet for same donation, Back to donations → root.



MyContributionsScreen — paginated from myContributionsProvider. Per item: donation title, formatted amount, status badge (PAID / PENDING / FAILED), contributionNumber, date. Filter chips: ALL / PAID / PENDING / FAILED.

State machine the app must enforce







Trigger



Verify response



UI





WebView returned to callback URL



not called yet



"Confirming…" overlay





Verify resolves status: "success"



any alreadyPaid



Success screen





Verify resolves status: "failed" | "abandoned"



—



Failed screen with Retry





Verify resolves status: "unknown"



—



Failed screen; Retry will re-verify





Verify network error after 3 retries



—



Failed screen; Retry still safe (idempotent)





User taps back during WebView



—



Call verify once before popping

Routing





/donations → DonationsListScreen



/donations/:id → DonationDetailsScreen



/donations/contributions → MyContributionsScreen



Transient pushes: DonationPaystackWebViewScreen, DonationSuccessScreen, DonationFailedScreen.

Add a "Donations" entry to the main drawer / bottom nav (wherever top-level destinations live).

FCM
Backend already pushes data.type === "DONATION_RECEIVED". In the existing FCM message handler, add a branch: when tapped, navigate to /donations/contributions. Do not use the FCM message to mark payment status — always go through the verify API.

UX / quality





Loading, empty, and error states for every screen.



All async work funneled through Riverpod — no setState for API state.



Disable buttons while requests are in flight; button-level spinners.



Currency via intl.NumberFormat.currency(name: 'ZAR', symbol: 'R ').



Dates via intl (d MMM yyyy, h:mm a).



Theming via Theme.of(context) — no hard-coded colors except status badge accents.



Accessibility: semantic labels on icons and CTAs.



Architecture: data → repository → providers → presentation. No HTTP calls from widgets.

Do NOT





Call Paystack REST directly from Flutter.



Store the Paystack secret or compute subunit amounts client-side.



Trust the WebView "success" URL alone — verify is mandatory.



Add new dependencies beyond webview_flutter if not already present.



Modify the existing API base URL / auth interceptor.



Edit any backend files.

Acceptance criteria





From DonationsListScreen, donate R 50 to any approved donation using Paystack test card 4084 0840 8408 4081 and reach DonationSuccessScreen with contributionNumber shown.



If the user closes the WebView mid-payment, verify is still called and the correct screen (Success or Failed) is shown.



Calling verify twice for the same reference returns alreadyPaid: true on the second call and the UI still shows Success without errors.



MyContributionsScreen shows the new PAID contribution at the top after a successful payment.



Filter chips on MyContributionsScreen work and pagination loads the next page.



All screens render correctly in light + dark themes.



flutter analyze is clean; dart format . applied.

Final step
After implementation, run flutter analyze and dart format ., report any remaining issues, and produce a short "How to test" checklist mirroring the acceptance criteria above.



End of Cursor prompt.

